[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: mswitch1
diagnosis_text:
The issue is not on router0. Router0’s VLAN-10 sub-interface is up and configured as the gateway: eth0.10 is UP with IP 172.16.10.1/24, and the kernel route for 172.16.10.0/24 points to eth0.10. PCs on VLAN 10 (pc4, pc5) show ARP “incomplete” for 172.16.10.1 and return “Destination Host Unreachable,” indicating L2 reachability to the gateway is broken, not that the gateway SVI is down.

Localization: On mswitch1 (the aggregation between switch1 and router0), the VLAN-10 subinterface on the uplink toward switch1 is DOWN: eth0.10@eth0 shows state DOWN. In contrast, VLAN-10 toward router0 is UP (eth4.10@eth4 UP), and VLAN-20 toward switch1 is UP (eth0.20 UP). This explains why Laptop0 on VLAN 20 is unaffected while VLAN 10 hosts at Location A cannot reach the gateway: VLAN 10 is severed only on the switch1-to-mswitch1 leg.

Mechanism: ARP requests from pc4/pc5 cannot traverse to the router0 SVI because mswitch1.eth0.10 (the tagged VLAN-10 on the link to switch1) is down, so no ARP replies reach the hosts.

Root cause: The VLAN-10 sub-interface mswitch1 eth0.10 on the trunk toward switch1 is down, isolating VLAN 10 from the routed core.

Corrective fix: Bring up mswitch1 eth0.10 and ensure it is enslaved to br_vlan10 and allowed on the trunk to switch1. Example: ip link set dev eth0.10 up; bridge link set dev eth0.10 master br_vlan10; verify tagging/allowed VLANs on that uplink. === END ===